IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`
IMPORT `er3-waiting-period`

-- Tests of er3-waiting-period (regulations 39 and 39.1). Every expected value is written by hand from the text
-- of regs 39 and 39.1 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 694-706) before the module was run. The day reg 39.1 came into
-- force is not in the text; the tests use 2020-01-01 as an invented stand-in and claim nothing about it.

-- The amount is followed by: a wage-loss plan for illness etc.; a workers' compensation plan; a 35(2)(f) indemnity; an employer's leave pay.
`test ordinary pay of 500` MEANS `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF 500, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`test wage-loss plan pay of 300` MEANS `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF 300, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`test workers' compensation of 200` MEANS `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF 200, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`test 35(2)(f) indemnity of 100` MEANS `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF 100, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`test employer leave pay of 50` MEANS `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF 50, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

§ `reg 39(3) -- amounts that are not counted`

#ASSERT `reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` `test ordinary pay of 500` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` `test wage-loss plan pay of 300` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` `test workers' compensation of 200` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` `test 35(2)(f) indemnity of 100` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` `test employer leave pay of 50` EQUALS TRUE
-- only the 500 of ordinary pay counts.
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) the earnings of the claimant during the waiting period` (LIST `test ordinary pay of 500`, `test wage-loss plan pay of 300`, `test workers' compensation of 200`, `test 35(2)(f) indemnity of 100`, `test employer leave pay of 50`) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) the earnings of the claimant during the waiting period` (LIST `test ordinary pay of 500`, `test ordinary pay of 500`) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) the earnings of the claimant during the waiting period` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§ `reg 39(1), (2) -- the deduction`

#ASSERT `reg 39(1) the amount to be deducted, before the limit of subsection (2)` 600 FALSE 0 EQUALS 600
-- paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) applies: the amount that paragraph requires, not the earnings.
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) the amount to be deducted, before the limit of subsection (2)` 600 TRUE 450 EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) the number of weeks of benefits from which the deduction is made` EQUALS 3
-- (2) not above the rate of weekly benefits (400): 600 is cut to 400; 300 stays; 400 is exactly the rate.
#ASSERT `reg 39(2) the amount deducted, not above the rate of weekly benefits` 600 400 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `reg 39(2) the amount deducted, not above the rate of weekly benefits` 300 400 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `reg 39(2) the amount deducted, not above the rate of weekly benefits` 400 400 EQUALS 400
-- (1), (2), (3) together.
#ASSERT `reg 39 the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks` (LIST `test ordinary pay of 500`, `test wage-loss plan pay of 300`) FALSE 0 400 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `reg 39 the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks` (LIST `test ordinary pay of 500`, `test wage-loss plan pay of 300`) FALSE 0 600 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `reg 39 the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks` (LIST `test ordinary pay of 500`) TRUE 250 400 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `reg 39 the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks` (LIST `test wage-loss plan pay of 300`, `test employer leave pay of 50`) FALSE 0 400 EQUALS 0

§ `reg 39.1 -- the waiting period is waived for an apprentice`

-- all three conditions; the earlier waiting period was served 2026-02-01, after the (stand-in) day of coming into force.
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- each condition missing in turn.
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- (c) the earlier waiting period must be served after the coming into force: the day itself is not after it (fork F10).
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 2) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2019 12 31) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
